<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seth</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seth was an ancient Egyptian god of storms, the desert, foreign lands and disorder. In myth he murdered his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osiris">Osiris</a> and fought Osiris's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horus">Horus</a> for the throne, but he also defended the sun god against the serpent Apophis. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> rulers honoured him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a>, and the Ramesside kings, among them Seti I, took their names from him.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>From around the 24th century BCE the god Osiris, a king murdered by his brother <b>Seth</b> and restored to life by his sister and wife Isis, rose to great importance as lord of the dead.</blockquote><a href="/religion/ancient-egyptian-religion">Ancient Egyptian religion · Origins</a></li><li><blockquote>The army fought in Nubia and the Levant: Ramesses II marched to the Battle of Kadesh in 1274 BCE with four divisions named after the gods Amun, Ra, Ptah and <b>Seth</b>.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ancient-egypt">Social Hierarchy of Ancient Egypt</a></li><li><blockquote>…Hussain Khan Bandanawazi, Farid Ayaz and Abu Muhammad Qawwal, Jafar Hussain Khan, the sitar and sarod players Ustad Vilayat Khan and Ustad Shujaat Khan, Zila Khan, the Nizami Bandhu, Hadiqa Kiani, Smita Bellur, Lata Mangeshkar, Asha Bhosle, Rahat Fateh Ali Khan, Kailash Kher, Kavita <b>Seth</b> and Maithili Thakur.</blockquote><a href="/songs/chhaap-tilak-sab-chheeni">Chhaap Tilak Sab Chheeni</a></li><li><blockquote>The Second Dynasty saw unrest, with Peribsen adopting <b>Seth</b> rather than Horus as his patron, before Khasekhemwy reunited the country.</blockquote><a href="/state/early-dynastic-egypt">Early Dynastic Egypt</a></li><li><blockquote>They worshipped <b>Seth</b>, identified with the storm god Baal, and traded widely with Canaan and Cyprus.</blockquote><a href="/state/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Fifteenth Dynasty of Egypt</a></li><li><blockquote>The best-attested king, Nehesy, whose name means 'the Nubian', left monuments at Avaris and Tell el-Muqdam and honoured <b>Seth</b> as lord of Avaris.</blockquote><a href="/state/fourteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Fourteenth Dynasty of Egypt</a></li></ul></section>
